<%= page_nav :home, "Home · HTMX on Rails" %>

<section class="hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Rails <%= Rails.version %> · htmx gem <%= htmx_gem_version %> · htmx 2</p>
  <h1>One HTML shell. Every page is a fragment.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The header, the tabs and this frame were rendered by Rails once. Each tab below
    asks the server for <strong>HTML</strong> and htmx swaps it into
    <code>#main-content</code> — no JSON, no client-side router, no state in the browser.
  </p>
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <%= htmx_link "About the gem", about_path, class: "button" %>
    <%= htmx_link "Contact form demo", contact_path, class: "button button-ghost" %>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="grid grid-2">
  <section class="card">
    <header class="card-head">
      <h2>Server clock</h2>
      <span class="tag">hx-trigger: every 2s</span>
    </header>
    <p>This fragment polls <code>/clock</code> every two seconds and replaces itself.</p>

    <%= render "pages/clock" %>

    <%= code_sample :clock %>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <header class="card-head">
      <h2>What the last tab click did</h2>
      <span class="tag">the gem</span>
    </header>
    <p>The tab links in the shell are built by the htmx gem — one hash, correct attributes:</p>

    <%= code_sample :nav %>

    <p>Rails answers with the fragment only. No layout, no head, no nav:</p>

    <%= code_sample :layout %>
  </section>
</div>

<section class="card">
  <header class="card-head">
    <h2>Four things to try</h2>
  </header>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <strong>Click a tab.</strong> Watch the URL change and the active tab update —
      the nav is refreshed out of band, the page is never reloaded.
      Reload the browser afterwards: you get the full page from the same URL.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Submit the contact form</strong> with an empty field, then with a valid
      one: a <code>422</code> renders the errors in place, a success response swaps the
      card and fires a toast from the <code>HX-Trigger</code> header.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Watch the clock.</strong> Each tick is a fresh request — the request id
      changes every two seconds.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Read the About page</strong> for the gem API: <code>HTMX[...]</code>,
      <code>HTMX.request</code> and <code>HTMX.response!</code>.
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>
